  "note": "The tuple schema states that its digest is SHA-256 over the RFC 8949 core deterministic CBOR encoding of the record with tuple_digest omitted, so that two implementations cannot disagree about the identity of a tuple. Nothing proved it. These two records hold identical values in opposite key order at every level; a reader that preserved insertion order would produce two digests and two identities for one certified tuple, which is the failure that would let a certification be evaded by re-serialising it.",
